{# Top-level comparison report. Every aggregate number carries a link to the task page,
   patch or grader log that supports it. See PLAN.md §4. #}
# Harness comparison — `{{ r.candidate_name }}` vs `{{ r.baseline_name }}`

| | |
|---|---|
| Run | `{{ r.run_id }}` |
| Created | {{ r.created_utc }} |
| Config | `{{ r.config }}` |
| Scale | {{ r.comparisons | length }} tasks × 2 harnesses × {{ r.reps }} reps = {{ r.comparisons | length * 2 * r.reps }} trials |

{% if r.jobs > 1 %}
> **Wall-clock is unreliable for this run.** It executed with `jobs={{ r.jobs }}`, so trials
> competed for the machine. Cost figures are unaffected; elapsed times are not comparable.

{% endif %}
## Recommendation: {{ r.recommendation.value }} — {{ r.confidence.value }} confidence

Decided by the first matching condition in the rule below. **Fired: `{{ r.rule_fired }}`**

The rule is evaluated top to bottom, first match wins. It is printed from the same ordered
list the code evaluates, so it cannot drift from the decision:

{% for line in r.rule_text %}
{{ loop.index }}. `{{ line }}`
{% endfor %}

Confidence is never reported as HIGH. A {{ r.comparisons | length }}-task suite cannot support
a strong claim in either direction.

{% if r.caveats %}
### Read this before acting on the above

{% for c in r.caveats %}
- {{ c }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Outcome per task

| Task | Baseline | Candidate | Transition | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for c in r.comparisons %}
| `{{ c.task_id }}` | {{ c.baseline.value }} | {{ c.candidate.value }} | {{ label[c.transition] }} | [detail]({{ task_link(c.task_id) }}) |
{% endfor %}

Counted: **{{ r.improvements | length }} improved**, **{{ r.regressions | length }} regressed**.
{% if r.unstable or r.unmeasured %}
{{ r.unstable | length }} unstable and {{ r.unmeasured | length }} unmeasured task(s) are
excluded from those counts — see below.
{% endif %}

{% if r.regressions %}
### Regressions

A task the baseline passed and the candidate failed. This outranks every other signal in the
rule above.

{% for c in r.regressions %}
- **`{{ c.task_id }}`** — [patches, grader logs and both arms' reps]({{ task_link(c.task_id) }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if r.unstable %}
## Unstable tasks — excluded from the counts

These tasks produced different outcomes across reps of the *same* harness. They are reported
separately rather than rounded to PASS or FAIL, because the reps did not agree and rounding
would manufacture a signal the evidence does not support.

{% for c in r.unstable %}
- **`{{ c.task_id }}`** — baseline {{ c.baseline.value }}, candidate {{ c.candidate.value }}
  — [per-rep breakdown]({{ task_link(c.task_id) }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if r.unmeasured %}
## Unmeasured tasks — excluded from the counts

No rep produced a trustworthy verdict, through infrastructure failure or a voided held-out
overlay. This is an absence of evidence, not evidence of a defect.

{% for c in r.unmeasured %}
- **`{{ c.task_id }}`** — [detail]({{ task_link(c.task_id) }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Dimensions

Tasks where **both** arms produced a verdict for that dimension. A half-measured task is not
counted, because "candidate 0/1" is indistinguishable from the candidate failing.

| Dimension | Graders | Baseline | Candidate | Δ | Self-consistent? |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for d in r.dimensions %}
| {{ d.dimension }} | {% for g in d.graders %}`{{ g }}`{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %} | {{ d.baseline_pass }}/{{ d.total }} | {{ d.candidate_pass }}/{{ d.total }} | {{ "%+d" | format(d.delta) }} | {% if d.noisy %}**no** — {{ d.baseline_unstable }} baseline / {{ d.candidate_unstable }} candidate task(s) flipped between reps{% else %}yes{% endif %} |
{% endfor %}

{% if r.dimensions | selectattr("noisy") | list %}
> A dimension marked **not self-consistent** disagreed with itself across reps of the same
> harness. Any delta on that row is at least partly noise and should not be read as a harness
> effect.

{% endif %}
{% if invariant %}
### Graders that never varied between the arms

These returned the same non-passing verdict in every trial of **both** harnesses, so they
carry no signal about the change under test — they cancel out of every delta above.

